    hs_sort_hb:"Latest heartbeat first",
    nt_hs:"Reads the Evernode host registrations from the Xahau ledger (the ledger side cannot tell which host you looked at). The rating is the score hosts give each other by testing every hour (0\u2013255); the price is EVR per hour (1 moment), with 30 days in brackets. CPU, memory and disk are the values the host registered; memory and disk are per instance (the total divided by the maximum number of instances). The spec class is (disk MB / 100 + memory MB + MHz \u00d7 cores) / 100 / max instances: 200 or more is Enterprise, 100 or more High end, 50 or more Medium, 20 or more Low end. Continuous uptime is not on the ledger, so look at days since registration and the last heartbeat (if it is older than the 1-hour window the host is stopped, and its VM may have a problem). Measurements are kept only on this device, for your own mailbox and the mailboxes you delivered letters to (nothing is sent anywhere).",
