      og_text:"Handpost has moved to handpost.page. This page still works for a while, but please move to the new place. How: on this page, ≡ → Account → [Link new device] → [Copy link text] → open the new place and paste it under Link this device → when the 6 digits appear, come back to this page and tap [Add]. Your address book is copied to the new place right away, and your past letters about 2 minutes later while this page stays open.", btn_og_open:"Open handpost.page",
      hs_perf_nt:"Spec is a per-instance guide (200+ Enterprise, 100+ High end, 50+ Medium, 20+ Low end, below that Lite). A low-end host is enough for a mailbox.", hs_perf_tip:"Spec = (CPU MHz × cores + RAM MB + disk MB ÷ 100) ÷ 100 ÷ max instances. 200+ Enterprise, 100+ High end, 50+ Medium, 20+ Low end, below that Lite",
      vt_sw_to_pk:"Switch to a passkey", vt_sw_to_pw:"Switch to a passphrase", vt_sw_pw:"Change the passphrase", vt_sw_note:"Before switching, your current protection is checked. If the switch fails, the current protection stays. Your paper backup (14 words) keeps working.", vt_sw_cur_pw:"Current passphrase", vt_sw_cur_pk:"Your current passkey is checked first, then the new protection is set.", btn_vt_sw_go:"Switch", btn_vt_sw_cancel:"Cancel", vt_sw_ok_pk:"Switched to a passkey. From the next time you open Handpost, the passkey opens it.", vt_sw_ok_pw:"Switched to a passphrase. From the next time you open Handpost, the passphrase opens it.", vt_sw_ok_pw2:"Passphrase changed. The new passphrase opens Handpost from next time.", vt_sw_oldpk:"Handpost cannot delete the previous passkey. Remove unused passkeys in this device's settings (Windows Hello, iCloud Keychain, etc.).", vt_e_sw_locked:"The keys are not open, so the protection cannot be switched.",
      rel_title:"Handpost version", rel_ok:"This is the latest official Handpost (version {n}). The developer's seal was verified ({t}).", rel_ok0:"This is the official Handpost. The developer's seal was verified ({t}).", rel_old:"This is the official Handpost, but an older version (open: version {o}, latest: version {n}). You can keep sending letters. Handpost reopens itself with the new version when nothing is being written. To update now, press [Reload].", rel_unknown:"The Handpost you have open does not match any official version (file that differed: {f}). Exchanges with mailboxes are stopped (letters are kept and waiting). Press [Reload]. If that does not help, turn off browser extensions and reopen, or tell the developer.", rel_served:"A file sent by the distribution site does not match the developer's seal ({f}). Exchanges with mailboxes are stopped (letters are kept and waiting). A new version may be in the middle of being published, so do not reload; wait a few minutes. Handpost checks again automatically and resumes when it matches. If this goes on, tell the developer.", rel_bad:"The list of files being distributed does not match the developer's seal. Exchanges with mailboxes are stopped (letters are kept and waiting). Do not reload; please tell the developer. It resumes automatically once the seal matches.", rel_bad_short:"Stopped: the developer's seal does not match", rel_nosig:"The distributed version has no developer's seal. Handpost will check again automatically. If this goes on, tell the developer.", rel_skip:"Not checked here (checked when opened at handpost.page).", rel_err:"Could not check ({e}). Check your connection. Handpost will check again automatically.", rel_wait:"Checking…", rel_note:"Handpost versions are protected by a seal (signature) made with the developer's key. Each time Handpost opens, and every 30 minutes while it is open, it checks that the files it loaded match an official version. Check number {fp} (for comparing with the developer). If the whole page were replaced by a fake, this display would be fake too, so this check alone cannot tell.", btn_rel_again:"Check again",
      rel_at:" (checked at {t})", rel_ext:"Besides Handpost, this page has {n} program(s) added by a browser extension or similar. The developer's seal does not cover them. Extensions can read the letters shown in Handpost, so turn off any extension you do not recognize in your browser settings.\n{list}", btn_rel_reload:"Reload",
    hist_wait:"Copying past letters from your other device ({dev}) is scheduled. They arrive through your mailbox about 2 minutes after Handpost is opened on {dev} (or right away over a direct link while both devices are open at the same time). (Tap to dismiss)",
